 "phrases": [
  "Can someone steal your money just by standing next to you?",
  "Let's look inside your card.",
  "Hidden in the plastic, there's a copper antenna. Wrapped around the edge, four times.",
  "And here's the weird part. Your card has no battery.",
  "So how does it talk to the reader?",
  "The reader creates a magnetic field. Invisible. Right here.",
  "When your card enters it, the field powers the antenna, and the chip wakes up.",
  "Then the chip does something clever. It creates a one-time code.",
  "That code only works for this payment. Never again.",
  "Approved. In a split second.",
  "But here's what thieves can actually do.",
  "A hidden reader, a few centimeters away, can read your card number. Sometimes the expiry date.",
  "But not your security code. And not that one-time code.",
  "So they can't copy your card to pay in a store.",
  "Do you need an RFID wallet? Not really. It's a cheap extra layer. Nothing more.",
  "Pop quiz: why does the reader need to be so close? Comment your answer.",
  "Follow Tech Unseen. Next lesson: is your phone secretly listening to you?"
 ],
